HST Office: light ribbon with the module colour only as a thin frame, the same on every backend.

- NotebookBar::UpdateBackground() (upstream) tints the whole notebookbar window with the module colour
  (Writer blue, Calc green, Impress orange; Misc/NotebookbarColorTransparency, upstream default 150).
  GTK (and Qt) draw the tab pane themselves with the theme's window colour, so the tint shows only as a thin
  frame around the ribbon. On macOS, Windows and the generic backend the pane is transparent, so the tint
  filled the whole ribbon (blue labels on blue, hard to read).
- vcl/source/control/tabctrl.cxx: for the Tabbed notebookbar's tab control on those backends, TabControl::Paint
  fills the tab strip with the dialog colour and the panel area with the window colour before the tabs are
  drawn. The tint stays visible only in the margin around the tab control, as on GTK. Colours come from the
  theme, so dark mode gives a dark panel with a subtle frame.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-defaults.py (tint value), tests/runtime/check-ribbon-panel.py (frame and panel colours).
